  "protocolVersion": null,
  "instructions": "Groundbox gives you sandboxes: private Linux VMs you run commands in, billed per second.\n\nTypical use: create_sandbox, then run_command as often as you like (git clone, install, tests), write_file and read_file to move files, and delete_sandbox when you are done. To give several agents the same ready environment, set one sandbox up and fork_sandbox it. After pushing to a repo that runs CI on Groundbox, wait_for_ci tells you pass or fail with the failing log.\n\nWith no API key, signup returns a key and a link a person must open to activate it.",
  "durationMs": 1947,
  "stderr": ""
